menu "M3U8 Parser Configuration"

    config M3U8_MAX_ITEMS
        int "Maximum number of segments/variants per playlist"
        default 16
        range 4 64
        help
            Maximum number of segments (media playlist) or variants (master playlist)
            that can be stored in a playlist structure.

            Typical values:
            - Audio streaming (live): 8-16 segments (1-2 minutes buffering)
            - Audio streaming (VOD): 16-32 segments
            - Video streaming: 32-64 segments

            Lower values = less RAM but may truncate large playlists.
            For HLS live audio, 16 segments is usually sufficient.

            RAM impact: each segment ~268 bytes, each variant ~332 bytes
            → 16 items ≈ 4.3-5.3 KB vs 32 items ≈ 8.6-10.6 KB

    config M3U8_MAX_URL_LENGTH
        int "Maximum URL length (bytes)"
        default 160
        range 64 512
        help
            Maximum length for segment/variant URLs.

            Typical values:
            - Short URLs (CDN): 128-160 bytes
            - Long URLs (query params): 256-384 bytes
            - Very long URLs: 512 bytes

            Most HLS URLs are under 200 bytes. For audio streaming with
            predictable CDN URLs, 160 bytes is usually sufficient.

            RAM impact: each segment/variant stores one URL
            → 160 bytes vs 256 bytes = -96 bytes per item
            → For 16 items: -1.5 KB savings

    config M3U8_MAX_CODEC_LENGTH
        int "Maximum codec string length (bytes)"
        default 32
        range 16 128
        help
            Maximum length for codec strings in variants (e.g., "mp4a.40.2").

            Typical values:
            - Audio only: 16-32 bytes (e.g., "mp4a.40.2")
            - Video + audio: 64-128 bytes (e.g., "avc1.4d401f,mp4a.40.2")

            For audio-only streaming, 32 bytes is sufficient.

            RAM impact: each variant stores one codec string
            → 32 bytes vs 64 bytes = -32 bytes per variant

    config M3U8_PARSER_DEBUG_LOGS
        bool "Enable detailed debug logs"
        default n
        help
            Enable verbose logging for M3U8 parsing (useful for debugging).
            Adds ~200 bytes code size.

endmenu
